# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction {#introduction}"
msgstr "Pendahuluan {#introduction}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The world is approaching the era of quantum advantage. Here, quantum advantage refers to executing a task on a hybrid quantum–classical system such that:\n"
"* The correctness of the output can be rigorously verified.\n"
"* The computation demonstrates a quantum separation &mdash; providing superior efficiency, cost-effectiveness, or accuracy compared with classical methods alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dunia sedang mendekati era quantum advantage. Di sini, quantum advantage merujuk pada menjalankan tugas pada sistem hybrid quantum–classical sedemikian rupa sehingga:\n"
"* Kebenaran outputnya dapat diverifikasi secara ketat.\n"
"* Komputasinya menunjukkan quantum separation &mdash; memberikan efisiensi, efektivitas biaya, atau akurasi yang lebih unggul dibanding metode klasik saja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reaching quantum advantage in the near term will require us to use every available tool to get the most out of today’s quantum hardware. In practice, that means confronting noise and errors head-on.\n"
"We have an ever-expanding toolkit to address these challenges, including error suppression, error mitigation, error detection, and error correction. These concepts can be difficult to distinguish, in part because they lie along a continuum on the path toward fault-tolerant quantum computing. Roughly speaking:\n"
"* Error suppression aims to reduce the probability of certain errors occurring in the first place.\n"
"* Error mitigation seeks to reduce the impact of errors that have occurred on the final result.\n"
"* Error detection and correction encode quantum information redundantly across multiple qubits, so that errors can be detected and corrected through consistency checks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mencapai quantum advantage dalam waktu dekat akan mengharuskan kita menggunakan setiap tool yang tersedia untuk memaksimalkan hardware quantum saat ini. Dalam praktiknya, itu berarti menghadapi noise dan error secara langsung.\n"
"Kita punya toolkit yang terus berkembang untuk mengatasi tantangan ini, termasuk error suppression, error mitigation, error detection, dan error correction. Konsep-konsep ini bisa sulit dibedakan, sebagian karena semuanya berada dalam satu kontinum menuju fault-tolerant quantum computing. Secara garis besar:\n"
"* Error suppression bertujuan mengurangi probabilitas terjadinya error tertentu sejak awal.\n"
"* Error mitigation berusaha mengurangi dampak error yang sudah terjadi terhadap hasil akhir.\n"
"* Error detection dan correction mengkodekan informasi quantum secara redundan di beberapa qubit, sehingga error dapat dideteksi dan dikoreksi melalui pemeriksaan konsistensi.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Image of errors being reduced by error suppression, then correction, then mitigation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/intro/error-handling.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Image of errors being reduced by error suppression, then correction, then mitigation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/intro/error-handling.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some techniques blur these boundaries. For example, if errors can be detected at the circuit level and invalid shots are discarded or probabilistically recovered in post-processing, this may be viewed as a limited form of error correction, though it lacks the full fault-tolerant structure of quantum error-correcting codes.\n"
msgstr "Beberapa teknik mengaburkan batasan-batasan ini. Misalnya, jika error bisa dideteksi di level circuit dan shot yang tidak valid dibuang atau dipulihkan secara probabilistik dalam post-processing, ini bisa dipandang sebagai bentuk terbatas dari error correction, meskipun tidak memiliki struktur fault-tolerant penuh dari kode error-correcting quantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling, another example, reshapes noise so that it behaves like a stochastic Pauli process. This can slow the buildup of coherent errors and make other techniques, such as error mitigation, more effective. On its own, however, it is best described as a form of noise tailoring, rather than strictly suppression or mitigation.\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling, contoh lainnya, mengubah bentuk noise sehingga berperilaku seperti proses Pauli stokastik. Ini bisa memperlambat penumpukan coherent error dan membuat teknik lain, seperti error mitigation, lebih efektif. Namun, jika berdiri sendiri, ini lebih tepat digambarkan sebagai bentuk noise tailoring, bukan murni suppression atau mitigation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These tools are not mutually exclusive. Effective workflows often combine multiple approaches. Suppression and mitigation are widely applicable today, while error detection can be used in some workflows to discard erroneous results or probabilistically recover correct states. Meanwhile, increasingly advanced forms of error correction are steadily coming within reach. By leveraging and combining these methods, we can build a continuous path toward fault-tolerant quantum computing. For a streamlined approach to leveraging multiple error mitigation techniques, without much theoretical background, see [this tutorial](/tutorials/combine-error-mitigation-techniques) on IBM Quantum&reg; Platform.\n"
msgstr "Tools ini tidak saling eksklusif. Workflow yang efektif sering menggabungkan beberapa pendekatan. Suppression dan mitigation sudah banyak diterapkan saat ini, sementara error detection bisa digunakan di beberapa workflow untuk membuang hasil yang keliru atau memulihkan state yang benar secara probabilistik. Sementara itu, bentuk-bentuk error correction yang semakin canggih perlahan mulai terjangkau. Dengan memanfaatkan dan menggabungkan metode-metode ini, kita bisa membangun jalur berkelanjutan menuju fault-tolerant quantum computing. Untuk pendekatan yang efisien dalam memanfaatkan beberapa teknik error mitigation, tanpa banyak latar belakang teori, lihat [tutorial ini](/tutorials/combine-error-mitigation-techniques) di IBM Quantum&reg; Platform.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this course, Tools for Quantum Advantage, we will explore some of the most promising methods for managing quantum noise and errors. Our focus is on exploring practical applications using Qiskit, while providing enough theoretical background to help you determine which techniques are appropriate for your use case. We will also highlight which methods can be combined effectively within a single workflow &mdash; and which ones typically cannot.\n"
msgstr "Dalam kursus ini, Tools for Quantum Advantage, kita akan menjelajahi beberapa metode paling menjanjikan untuk menangani quantum noise dan error. Fokus kita adalah mengeksplorasi penerapan praktis menggunakan Qiskit, sambil memberikan cukup latar belakang teori untuk membantu kamu menentukan teknik mana yang cocok untuk kasus penggunaanmu. Kita juga akan menyoroti metode mana yang bisa digabungkan secara efektif dalam satu workflow &mdash; dan mana yang biasanya tidak bisa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Join us as we explore the tools that will help bring quantum advantage within reach.\n"
msgstr "Yuk ikuti kita menjelajahi tools yang akan membantu mewujudkan quantum advantage.\n"
